 Assessment of the South Lincoln Waste Site – Environmental Impact Assessment (EIA)
This CASStudie has three objectives, these being to provide the National Policy Framework for a South Lincoln Waste Transfer Station and to inform ongoing discussions on this subject by providing a report analysing its environmental impacts. Additionally it seeks to raise awareness among all stakeholders that planning permission must be refused to any proposal for a new Transfer Station in south Lincoln; a refusal that will ensure that future development, associated with a Transfer Station, is focused on alternative sites better suited to Lincoln's communities’ needs.
• to provide an initial assessment of those aspects which may give rise to significant adverse impacts;
• to analyse the risks involved in any such project;
• to define a range of alternatives to accommodate expected levels of demand for local refuse collection;
• to consider whether disposal is appropriate in any of these places;
• to recommend further actions (eg: site remediation, public/private infrastructure) to reduce, manage / mitigate and compensate for those issues
